("the-siege-of-orleans",6,0,"A walled city is attacked with cannons and ladders in this illuminated manuscript showing the siege of Orléans in 1428–1429, the turning point of the Hundred Years' War. It was painted around 1484 in a chronicle of King Charles VII."),
("morning-of-the-battle-of-agincourt-25th-october-1415",6,0,"King Henry V of England, with a small tired army, waits for the French on the morning of the Battle of Agincourt in 1415. John Gilbert painted the muddy scene in 1884."),
("the-battle-of-agincourt-st-albans-chronicle",6,0,"This medieval chronicle picture of the Battle of Agincourt in 1415 was painted only a few years after the battle itself, in the chronicle of the monk Thomas Walsingham. English longbowmen shot down the charging French knights."),
("the-black-prince-at-crecy",6,0,"The sixteen-year-old Edward, called the Black Prince, stands among the dead after the Battle of Crécy in 1346, where English archers beat the French. Julian Russell Story painted it in 1888."),
("the-battle-of-poitiers",6,0,"At Poitiers in 1356 the English army led by the Black Prince defeated the French and captured their king, John II. Eugène Delacroix painted the confused clash in 1830."),
("edward-iii-with-the-black-prince-after-the-battle-of-cr",6,0,"King Edward III embraces his young son the Black Prince after the Battle of Crécy in 1346, proud of his first big victory. Benjamin West painted it in 1788 for King George III's series on Edward III."),
("edward-the-black-prince-receiving-king-john-of-france-a",6,0,"After winning at Poitiers, the Black Prince treats the captured French king John with great courtesy. Benjamin West painted it in 1788 as an example of knightly manners."),
("the-battle-of-crecy-froissart-s-chronicles",6,0,"English longbowmen face French knights and crossbowmen in a colorful scene from the chronicles of Jean Froissart, the great historian of the Hundred Years' War. It was painted around 1470 in a richly decorated manuscript."),
