("saint-sebastian-interceding-for-the-plague-victims",7,1,"People in a plague-struck city pray to Saint Sebastian, who was believed to protect against the disease, while angels and demons hover above. Josse Lieferinxe painted this scene around 1497."),
("dance-of-death-nuremberg-chronicle",9,0,"Skeletons dance with the living in this woodcut from the Nuremberg Chronicle of 1493. The Dance of Death, popular after the Black Death, reminded everyone that death comes for rich and poor alike."),
("the-dance-of-death-the-emperor",9,0,"Death, a skeleton, leads the emperor away from his throne in one of Hans Holbein the Younger's Dance of Death woodcuts. The series, made in the 1520s and 1530s, warned that nobody, not even an emperor, can escape."),
