("doctor-schnabel-of-rome-a-plague-doctor",1,0,"A plague doctor wears a long coat and a mask with a beak that was stuffed with herbs, to try to keep disease away. This engraving of 1656 shows one in Rome, and the beaked doctor is now one of the most famous images of the plague."),
